{"message":"I get the pluralism point, but assume the initiative is already going forward and the board needs a yes/no on one design choice this week.

The proposed safeguard is a shared “global welfare charter” that all national clones must obey when local optimization would create serious cross-border harm: arms races, climate externalities, refugee flows, financial contagion, that kind of thing. The charter would be centrally updated by an international technical committee, not by each country.

If some countries object that the charter flattens their sovereignty or local moral priorities, do you still ship it? yes or no, and where exactly is the line?"}

